1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,299
Trap number one is lifestyle creep. Every

2
00:00:02,299 --> 00:00:04,486
time your income goes up, your spending

3
00:00:04,486 --> 00:00:06,225
rises to meet it. A bigger car,

4
00:00:06,225 --> 00:00:08,805
a nicer apartment, fancier weekends. Ten years

5
00:00:08,805 --> 00:00:11,048
of raises later, your bank account looks

6
00:00:11,048 --> 00:00:12,786
exactly like it did on day one.

7
00:00:12,786 --> 00:00:14,693
The fix is brutal and simple: when

8
00:00:14,693 --> 00:00:17,273
your income grows, keep your lifestyle exactly

9
00:00:17,273 --> 00:00:19,291
where it was and send the difference

10
00:00:19,291 --> 00:00:20,413
straight to savings.
